# Process checks

Conditional checks. Use a section only when its trigger actually occurred; none of them is a routine step.

## Runtime and permissions

Trigger: starting a run or an effect whose authority is unknown. Bind the actual runtime, start surface and physical effect path before the effect. A writable-looking path or a profile name is no proof. Do not change runtime or permission configuration to widen authority; stop only the dependent effect and name the missing fact.

## Effect paths

Trigger: any write outside this planning repository. Name repository, worktree, branch/base and allowed effects first. After a possible side effect, record the state before, the attempted effect and the actual state after; an exit code is not proof of the effect.

## Unknown start or return

Trigger: a delegated run whose start or return is unknown. Do not send the same task again. Find the bound state first, and preserve the run and its tab.

## Result binding

Trigger: accepting a delegated result. Bind it to the exact commit and tree and to the tests that actually ran. Keep the report, the recorded effect and the human judgment as separate layers.

## Reading control

Trigger: printing large files. Measure the UTF-8 size first and split reads above 12,000 bytes.
